        "q": "My DEXA scan was normal. Does that mean my bones are fine?",
        "a": "It means your bone density is in the normal range, which is good news and not the whole picture. In type 1 diabetes, fracture risk is consistently higher than density alone predicts - in one study of postmenopausal women, density was identical to matched controls while fracture history was far more common. The difference appears to sit in the quality and structure of bone, which a standard scan is not measuring. A normal result is worth having; it is not a guarantee, and it is a reasonable thing to ask your clinician about in the context of your diabetes rather than on its own."
